    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to another episode of Elictable, sponsored by Indiana Women's Action Movement. Today, we are just honored to have US Representative Frank Mervain join us to talk about the protection of the rights to organize the pro act and and I know there are some kind of logistical details that I hope you'll help us with too because I know that it passed last year as a bill but now there's a new version that I think we're hoping to get passed still but but generally the topic of unions is very important to the first congressional district as it is to all losers and I'd like to just remind people that who's unions were what created the middle class in this country. That was how parents were able to raise children, buy a home, buy a car, go on vacation, send their children to college. And like all parents, you know, you want to be able to provide a little more for your kids than you had. And so this was really important. And this is what created the middle class. And as we all know, our economy depends on consumer spending. And that is really one of the biggest drivers. And of course, unions really supported that model as well. And so then over the years, we had laws adopted Indiana being one of the first, I think, of the 27 states now to pass the right to work law, which specifically just said that if you worked somewhere that had a union, You didn't have to pay dues, but you still got the benefit of the union. So that was kind of interesting. And it really did it away with a lot of union rights. So anyway, sorry, I want you to get into this conversation, Representative Burban. I'm so sorry. So welcome. And tell us, you know, tell us your background and why you believe in unions, because I know you do.",
