  {
    "episode_id": 72630,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72630.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well, I guess my first question is, this is so timely. We're seeing all these kinds of cultural phenomenon happening now where people have been off and everybody's looking for people to work, looking for workers everywhere. They can't find people. And people, I think, are in a moment where they're saying, I'm not going back to that old system. where I was underpaid, I couldn't even afford childcare, I couldn't afford to make a living. And I don't want to go back to working for jobs so that I can support my kids. And so I think this is just such an important moment. And I hope that we can bring this education to people who are in a position now to make some demands. and get this bill passed, and people will be able to bring their rights up in employment and make their jobs better and make it better to work. So I don't know, what do you think about the timing of all this?",
