  {
    "episode_id": 72630,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72630.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, the words of wisdom. One, I want to thank you for being engaged and having the insight to understand that this is an extremely important issue for our region for Northwest Indiana, the state of Indiana, and also the United States of America, making sure that men and women who are working every single day have the right to organize, have the right to make a fair wage. As you mentioned, have the ability to break through into the middle class by having creating an opportunity to throw this through the pro act, which protects unionization and allows opens the door for a fair election in a union. That is extremely important to us here as a member of Congress and my staff. I'm on the education and labor committee. And so we're working hard every single day on committee and on bills that will enhance and protect unions and protect our manufacturing based on our domestic steel industries. And that being said, you're absolutely right. It has to do with the service unions. It has to do with the teachers unions. It has to do with the electrical unions. It has to do with the steel workers, the BPM equal workers, the iron workers, the construction trades, the brick layers, the teachers, all those individuals who have been chipped away And the unionization has been chipped away from we have to stand up and we have to stand up for workers to close that equity gap and to make sure people have a fair opportunity to make a living provide for their children and have a good quality of life. And so it is a moment in time. that is recognizable that we have to act and we have to turn, make sure that we produce deliverables that enhance and empower the middle class and our union member brothers and sisters to have the most advantage that they possibly can to have a safe work force, to have a safe work environment, to be able to collectively bargain and to be able to receive a pension at the end of the day that they were promised.",
